course: dictionary
lesson: 4143
title: The glossary
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A glossary is a list of hard or special words with their meanings, usually at the back of a book. It is like a small dictionary just for that one book or topic. «A glossary is a list of key words and their meanings, usually at the back of a non-fiction book.»
explain: In non-fiction and science books, key words are often printed in bold. If you meet one you do not know, check the glossary before you read on. Ali skipped the glossary and got stuck on «hibernate», so he lost the thread of the page.
explain: Ali should have looked it up in the glossary. «Hibernate» means a long winter sleep, so once he knew that, he could keep reading. When you learn a new key word, you can add it to the glossary too.
fact: A glossary is a list of key words and their meanings.
fact: A glossary is usually found at the back of a non-fiction book.
fact: A glossary is like a small dictionary just for one book or topic.
fact: Key words in bold are often explained in the glossary.
fact: «Look it up in the glossary» means check the meaning of a word there, and «add to the glossary» means write a new word and its meaning in the list.
exercise: Where is a glossary usually found in a book? | On the cover of a magazine | *At the back of a non-fiction book | At the front of a storybook
exercise: Ali gets stuck on «hibernate». What should he do first? | *Look it up in the glossary | Ask for a different book | Skip the page and never read it | Guess that it means a loud noise
exercise: What does «hibernate» mean? | A type of cold drink | A loud cheer | *A long winter sleep | A quick run around the park
test: A glossary is most like which of these? | A diary of your day | A map of the world | *A small dictionary for one book or topic
test: What kinds of words does a glossary explain? | Names of your classmates | *Hard or special words from a non-fiction book | Words from a song you know
exam: Why is a glossary helpful when you read a science book? | *It explains the bold key words, so you can keep reading | It lets you skip every hard word for ever | It is a list of your favourite songs | It tells you how the book ends
